My thoughts of this project


Backend:
    - Has a listener that picks up received emails that are directed to a specific email address
        Raw emails are stored in database for tracking and audit purposes, they have an id that is linked to a processed email
    - The email is parsed into readable data
    - Backend consists of json configurable guide that gives instructions to AI agent on how to review the email and respond
        Guide gives clear instructions on what to do and what details are potentially important (Order ID, Error message) 
    - Parsed email and a guide is provided to an AI agent
        Only accept AI response in processable data, if AI does not provide data in desired state, log the bad response and query the agent again
    - AI agent responds in a format that is then processed and stored in the database

Frontend:
- Reads database and provides details to user
- Categorised emails are displayed in a list with details
   User can click on an email to manage it
   User can view the original email
   User can accept the AI response and send it to the customer
   User can edit the AI response and send it to the customer
   User can view the audit trail
- User can view/edit the guide and save it

